    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive profile, anchored by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (76.77) and **Yordan Alvarez** (73.33). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our premier play, benefiting from a favorable matchup against Roupp and an elite, speed-optimized role atop the order; his ability to exploit a 1.88s catcher pop time makes him the primary engine for our stolen base targets. **Trea Turner** (70.35) and **Kyle Schwarber** (68.40) also project as elite starts against Eisert; **Trea Turner** specifically benefits from a slow SP delivery that maximizes his stolen base potential, while **Kyle Schwarber** leverages a significant platoon advantage and leadoff positioning. **Christian Yelich** (73.12) remains a locked-in utility start, with high park factors and an assumed leadoff role boosting his efficiency well into the elite tier.\n\nWe are navigating several \"Lineup Pending\" designations, most notably for **Gary Sanchez**, **Caleb Durbin**, **Junior Caminero**, **Carson Benge**, and **Christian Yelich**. While **Junior Caminero** faces a tougher matchup against the 3.45 xERA of Bachar, his projection remains a solid 58.70 thanks to his dynamic platoon profile and expected #2 hole. The most difficult bench decision involved **Nelson Velazquez** (56.76), whose elite 0.478 xwOBA makes him a formidable weapon. However, he ultimately lost his spot to the high-efficiency matchup of **Luke Raley** (64.85), who benefits from a generous SP xERA of 4.54 and positive park/wind conditions. **Colt Keith** (55.09) also lingered near the threshold but was edged out by the superior daily efficiency scores assigned to our infield starters.\n\nRisks today are primarily concentrated in the bottom half of the lineup where **Dillon Dingler** (43.78) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (45.72) face steeper pitching challenges. **Dillon Dingler** is hampered by a significant negative platoon adjustment against Miller, while **Kazuma Okamoto** faces a stiff test against the 3.62 xERA of Bradish. We will monitor weather reports for potential wind shifts, as our current scores rely heavily on the +5% wind-out bonuses calculated for our outfielders and **Chase Meidroth** (57.69). All managers should remain alert for official lineup cards, as any unexpected drop to the bottom of the order for our middle-of-the-road starters like **Gary Sanchez** could necessitate a pivot to our bench depth.",
